  "RETURN TYPES: levenshtein/editdist3/damerau_levenshtein/hamming/mismatches -> BIGINT; jaccard -> DOUBLE (typeof probes).",
  "NULL: any NULL argument (either or both positions) -> NULL for all six functions; typeof still resolves to BIGINT/DOUBLE.",
  "CASE: all case-sensitive. levenshtein('A','a')=1, editdist3=1, damerau=1, hamming=1, jaccard('A','a')=0.0.",
  "editdist3 IS levenshtein: 200-random-pair sweep 0 diffs; both equal plain-Levenshtein python reference on all 200; identical results on unicode witnesses ('\\u00e9','e')=2 and astral=4.",
  "damerau_levenshtein is the UNRESTRICTED Damerau-Levenshtein (NOT OSA/restricted), transposition cost 1: ('ca','abc')=2 (OSA would be 3), ('ab','ba')=1, ('a cat','an act')=2; 300-pair sweep: 0 diffs vs unrestricted-DL reference, 3 diffs vs OSA, 5 vs plain lev; OSA-refuting pairs pinned individually: ('aca','aabbc')=3, ('cbbac','abcb')=3, ('ab','bcca')=3 (OSA says 4 for each).",
  "jaccard: SET of single BYTES (not bigrams, not codepoints), duplicates ignored, |A&B|/|A|B|: ('ab','ba')=1.0, ('aab','ab')=1.0, ('abc','abd')=0.5 (bits 3fe0000000000000; bigram model would give 1/3).",
